WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.381
- [Narrator] In this curious
lagoon, the rivers may run red,

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:08.241
but rest assured, it's water, not blood.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:12.408
Although you could be forgiven
for confusing the two.

00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:19.876
The red lagoon is located
12,000 feet above sea level,

00:00:19.876 --> 00:00:21.960
in an area of Chile so remote,

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.680
that it wasn't even known by
the National Tourism Office

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.597
until 2009.

00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:29.934
And maybe that's a good thing,

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.621
because much like the pyramids in Egypt,

00:00:31.621 --> 00:00:34.301
the lagoon is believed to be cursed.

00:00:34.301 --> 00:00:37.344
Legend says that the waters
are owned by the devil himself,

00:00:37.344 --> 00:00:40.144
and he is responsible for
the mysterious disappearances

00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:42.725
that have occurred along the shores.

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:44.941
The thermal temperatures of the water,

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:46.901
at 100 to 120 degrees,

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:49.803
stop even wild animals
from approaching it.

00:00:49.803 --> 00:00:52.762
Devils aside, what causes
this blood-red water?

00:00:52.762 --> 00:00:55.621
Well, biologists studying
the lagoon recently traced it

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:59.102
to algae growing in
the depths of the lake.

00:00:59.102 --> 00:01:02.601
Still, much of this
lagoon remains a mystery.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.639
A visit to this place is a
reminder that there's still

00:01:05.639 --> 00:01:08.389
much to marvel at on this planet.

